messages:
marie: FYI ran into a subtle Android-only issue: Retrofit + OkHttp + authenticator = duplicated uploads when the RequestBody is streaming and the connection is retried. Repro in our sample with video upload + 401 refresh flow.
jasper: oh no. Is this the non-repeatable RequestBody problem?
marie: yup. Steps: 1) POST streaming body -> server resets connection mid-upload -> OkHttp retries/recovers -> authenticator kicks in on 401 -> we end up sending the body twice or failing midway depending on device.
own: Which client config? retryOnConnectionFailure? connectionPool?
marie: default client, so retryOnConnectionFailure=true. We're using an Authenticator that does a blocking token refresh and returns a new request with Authorization header. Code snippet:
```java
Authenticator a = (route, response) -> {
  synchronized (refreshLock) {
    if (isRefreshing) return null;
    isRefreshing = true;
    try {
      String t = tokenRefresher.blockingRefresh();
      return response.request().newBuilder().header("Authorization","Bearer "+t).build();
    } finally { isRefreshing = false; }
  }
};
```
jasper: authenticator throwing in with retryOnConnectionFailure can be tricky because OkHttp may attempt to recreate the request. call.clone() does not make a streaming RequestBody repeatable.
own: Observed mostly on older devices (API 22-24) and when we stream from InputStream or ContentResolver. Buffered bodies avoid it.
marie: short-term fixes we tested: 1) set retryOnConnectionFailure(false) on OkHttpClient to avoid hidden retries; 2) make RequestBody repeatable by buffering to temp file or byte[]; 3) move token refresh out of Authenticator into an Interceptor that ensures you only retry when you can rebuild the body.
jasper: moving to an interceptor is nice because you can surface 401 to the app and let it re-submit a fresh repeatable request, but UX impact on mobile. Also memory trade-offs for buffering.
own: code helper we used in sample to make a repeatable body via temp file:
```java
static RequestBody fileBacked(InputStream in, MediaType mt) throws IOException {
  File f = File.createTempFile("upload", "tmp", context.getCacheDir());
  try (OutputStream os = new FileOutputStream(f)) {
    byte[] buf = new byte[8192];
    int r;
    while ((r = in.read(buf)) != -1) os.write(buf,0,r);
  }
  return RequestBody.create(mt, f);
}
```
marie: We also added a small instrumented test in android-samples that simulates Connection: reset and asserts only one upload attempt reaches the fake server.
jasper: We should document best practices in the SDK docs: "+notes on non-repeatable bodies + authenticators", and a sample toggle for retryOnConnectionFailure. Also suggest logging a warning in the SDK when an authenticator is set and the request body appears non-repeatable.
own: CI bot created issue #3570: "android-sdk: mitigate duplicate streaming uploads when using Authenticator + OkHttp retries" https://github.com/redwood-inference/android-samples/issues/3570 :robot_face:
marie: I'll draft the sample PR (temp-file option + doc blurb) and add an opt-in lint rule for developers to catch streaming RequestBody + authenticator combos. Tagging @jasper @owen for review. Thanks :thumbsup:
